{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>By the way of the wilderness, the Sea of Reeds.</b> That they would go to the Sea of Reeds by way of the wilderness, for by that route no informers would come from Egypt, and they would not know of Pharaoh's pursuit until he overtook them, as it says: וַיִּשְׂאוּ בְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל אֶת עֵינֵיהֶם, וְהִנֵּה מִצְרַיִם וְכוּ׳ (Exodus 14:10). And at that point there was no remedy for them in turning back, for Pharaoh and his army would not receive them." "<b>And chamushim they went up.</b> And all this was necessary to do even though they were armed — for despite all their weaponry they had no courage of heart to do battle with the Egyptians and escape, for they had not been tested in these."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:25:22.077043821Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}